  "response_text": "The Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) is a software interface that standardizes interaction between application code and hardware peripherals. Rather than requiring low-level register manipulation, HAL functions allow configuration and control of features such as timers, digital I/O, and communication protocols. This abstraction simplifies firmware development, enhances portability across different microcontroller platforms, and improves code maintainability by isolating hardware-specific details.\\n",
